     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-top:1em;margin-bottom:1em;line-height:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;font-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;\">Hello!</p><p style=\"margin-top:1em;margin-bottom:1em;line-height:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;font-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;\"><span style=\"text-align:center\">I’m using this package for my thesis about wild boar&#39;s home range. I turned the dataset into a Move object with the package ‘Move’. I think that part of the process and the result are not exact and I’m looking for the problem. I noticed that in the first scatter plot, with telemetry object, the locations are represented by circles of different size and not points like in the Buffalo example. Could it be a </span><span style=\"text-align:center\">problem? How can I fix it?</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:1em;margin-bottom:1em;line-height:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;font-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;\"><span style=\"text-align:center\">Thank you</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:1em;margin-bottom:1em;line-height:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;font-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;\"><span style=\"text-align:center\">Silvia</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:1em;margin-bottom:1em;line-height:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;font-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;\"><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/ctmm-user/attach/5454d2fb103ca/Rplot.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"Rplot.png\" width=\"320\" height=\"232\" style=\"text-align:center;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\"></p><p style=\"margin-top:1em;margin-bottom:1em;line-height:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;font-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;\"><br></p></div>"
